-- run: an IMPORTED record alias's constructor builds the RECORD (backend.md
-- §4's record-alias row, D12), with the same keys as its local twin: interface
-- v3 carries the alias's field names (checker-v2.md §14.2, CK-39), so
-- `Debug.toString (P 1 "a")` prints the record. Until R3 this was
-- `build/bad/RecordAliasConstructorImported`: refused at emit with
-- `not_implemented` at `P`, because interface v2 had no field names and writing
-- 7427828's tagged object would have given one type two shapes at run time.
-- Oracle twin: the local alias (`run/RecordAliasConstructor.beni`) prints the
-- record the same way.
import Node exposing (Program)
import Pt exposing (P)


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines [ Debug.toString (P 1 "a") ]
